{"id": "glm2_frog_jumps_k_mod", "signature": "solve(n, k)", "statement": "A frog climbs a staircase of n steps, taking any number of steps from 1 to k at a time. Return the number of distinct ordered sequences of jumps whose values sum exactly to n, modulo 1000000007. There is exactly 1 way for n = 0 (the empty sequence); if n is negative return 0; k is a positive integer.", "tests": [{"args": [0, 2], "expected": 1}, {"args": [3, 2], "expected": 3}, {"args": [4, 2], "expected": 5}, {"args": [5, 3], "expected": 13}, {"args": [1, 1], "expected": 1}, {"args": [-2, 3], "expected": 0}, {"args": [10, 4], "expected": 401}, {"args": [30, 3], "expected": 53798080}, {"args": [100, 2], "expected": 782204094}, {"args": [0, 3], "expected": 1}, {"args": [7, 5], "expected": 61}, {"args": [6, 6], "expected": 32}, {"args": [15, 4], "expected": 10671}], "facts": [["arg", "n", "int"], ["arg", "k", "int"], ["items_range", "1", "k"], ["target", "n"], ["ask", "count_ways"], ["order", "matters"], ["modulo", "1000000007"]], "deps": {"schema": ["range_steps"], "uses": ["range_steps"], "solution_sha256": "200d8a5ead8aa08d3151c11a2d8786af62c139ad8dde50895b1ddea420fe3e89", "reference_sha256": "8f14373c5f52ce7a77929eb1311f2cb11926b8dae6bb658513c6c722b0976238"}}